# Brightwater Family Law — Build Specification

This document is the single source of truth for building this site. Follow it precisely. Do not introduce design decisions (colors, fonts, layout patterns, component styles) that aren't specified here. Where something is ambiguous, default to restraint and simplicity over decoration.

---

## 1. Project overview

A single, long-form scrolling page for a fictional boutique family law firm in Brisbane (also serving the Gold Coast). The visitor is almost always a stressed, anxious, first-time legal client researching late at night. The entire page exists to do three things, in priority order:

1. Build instant trust (calm, human, premium-but-approachable — never cold, corporate, or aggressive)
2. Communicate expertise within seconds
3. Drive one specific action: **booking a free 20-minute consultation**

This is a single-page site. No multi-page routing. No nav links to separate pages — nav links scroll to in-page sections.

---

## 2. Tech stack

- **React 18 + TypeScript**
- **Vite** as the build tool
- **Tailwind CSS** for styling — all colors, fonts, and spacing must be defined as Tailwind theme tokens (see Section 3), not arbitrary inline hex values scattered through components
- No UI component library (no shadcn, no MUI, no Chakra). Build components from scratch using Tailwind. This site needs a custom, designed feel — not a library's default look.
- No backend/database needed. The booking section will embed a Calendly inline widget (script tag + div, provided separately) — no custom booking logic needs to be written.
- Deploy target: static build, deployable to Vercel or Netlify.

