## 3. Design system (do not deviate from this)

### Colors — add these to `tailwind.config` as custom theme colors

```
cream:        #F6F2EA   (primary background)
sand:         #EAE4D2   (secondary/alternating section background)
sage:         #4F6B58   (primary accent — CTAs, key icons, links, headline highlights)
sage-dark:    #33433A   (darker accent — stronger section backgrounds, hover states)
charcoal:     #22211C   (primary text color — NEVER use pure black #000000)
charcoal-soft:#5B5848   (secondary/muted text color — NEVER use generic gray #888 or #999)
```

Rules:
- Background is never pure white. Use `cream` as the default page background.
- Alternate `cream` and `sand` (or `sage-dark`) between sections to create rhythm without introducing new colors.
- `sage` is the ONE dominant accent color. It is used for: primary CTA buttons, key icons, link hover states, occasional headline emphasis. Do not introduce a second accent color (no blue, no gold, no red) anywhere on the site.
- Text uses `charcoal` (primary) and `charcoal-soft` (secondary) only. Never pure black, never default Tailwind gray-500/gray-600/etc.
- No gradients anywhere. No drop shadows except very subtle ones on cards (max `shadow-sm` equivalent, low opacity, warm-tinted not gray-tinted if customized).

### Typography

- **Headings**: Lora, weight 700 (bold). Import from Google Fonts. Use for all h1/h2/h3 and major section headlines.
- **Body & UI text**: Public Sans, weights 400 and 500 only. Use for paragraphs, nav, buttons, labels, form fields.
- Do NOT use Inter anywhere — it is explicitly excluded from this project.
- Hero headline (h1) should be large and confident: minimum `text-4xl` on mobile, scaling up to `text-5xl` or `text-6xl` on desktop. The headline must feel commanding, not timid — err toward bigger/bolder rather than safe/small.
- Section headlines (h2) should be clearly hierarchical below the hero but still substantial — `text-3xl`/`text-4xl` range.
- Body text: `text-base` to `text-lg`, line-height relaxed (`leading-relaxed` or `leading-7`) for readability, especially on mobile.
- Sentence case throughout. No ALL CAPS except small tracked-out labels (e.g. "FAMILY LAW" under the logo, or small eyebrow labels above section headlines) — and even those should be used sparingly.

### Logo / header lockup

- Icon: a provided abstract wave/arc SVG or PNG asset (will be supplied separately) representing calm water/horizon. Single color, sage green.
- Wordmark: "Brightwater" rendered as LIVE TEXT in Lora 700, not as part of an image. "Family Law" or "FAMILY LAW" as a smaller tracked-out label in Public Sans underneath or beside it.
- Header layout: icon + wordmark on the left, nav links + primary CTA button on the right (desktop). On mobile: icon + wordmark on the left, hamburger menu icon on the right — collapse nav links into the mobile menu.
- Header should be sticky on scroll, with a subtle background (cream, possibly with a soft bottom border) so it stays usable as the visitor scrolls the long page.

### Buttons

- Primary CTA button: `sage` background, cream/white text, generous horizontal padding (e.g. `px-6 py-3`), rounded corners (`rounded-lg`, not fully pill-shaped, not sharp corners), medium font weight. Hover state: slightly darker sage (`sage-dark`) or a subtle scale/opacity transition — keep it understated, not bouncy or flashy.
- There should be only ONE primary CTA style used consistently everywhere: "Book your free consultation" (or equivalent short, consistent wording). Do not introduce multiple different-looking buttons for the same action.
- Secondary actions (if any — e.g. "Learn more" anchor links) should look visually subordinate: outline style, text link with arrow, or ghost button — never competing visually with the primary CTA.

### Spacing & layout

- Generous whitespace between sections — this site should never feel cramped or dense. Minimum vertical section padding: `py-16` on mobile, `py-24` or more on desktop.
- Max content width: constrain text-heavy content to a readable measure (e.g. `max-w-3xl` for paragraphs, `max-w-6xl` or `max-w-7xl` for full section containers/grids).
- Mobile-first: design and test every section at mobile width first (375px–428px range), then scale up. Most of Brightwater's real-world traffic is mobile — this is a hard requirement, not a nice-to-have.
- No dense multi-column layouts on mobile — stack everything vertically, single column, generous tap targets (min 44px height for interactive elements).

### Imagery

- No stock photos of gavels, scales of justice, courtrooms, or handshake clichés.
- Prefer warm, human, candid-feeling photography (people in calm settings, soft natural light) OR tasteful abstract/illustrative elements (e.g. soft wave/line motifs echoing the logo) over generic corporate stock photography.
- If real photography isn't available/sourced yet, use warm-toned placeholder blocks (sand or sage-tinted) with a label, rather than defaulting to harsh gray placeholder boxes.

### Icons

- If icons are needed (e.g. for the practice area cards or process steps), use a single consistent icon set (e.g. Lucide React or Tabler icons), outline style only, sage-colored, never filled/solid style icons, never mixed icon sets.

