## 4. Page structure (build in this exact order)

This is a single page, top to bottom. Each section is described with its purpose, content, and key design notes.

### 1. Header (sticky)
Logo lockup left, nav links (e.g. "Practice areas", "About", "FAQ") + primary CTA button right. Mobile: hamburger menu.

### 2. Hero section
- Large, confident Lora headline speaking directly to the visitor's emotional state (calm, reassuring, human — not a firm-name-first headline). Example direction: "You don't have to figure this out alone."
- Short supporting subhead in Public Sans (1–2 sentences) introducing what the firm does and the free consultation offer.
- Primary CTA button visible immediately, above the fold on mobile.
- Background: cream, possibly with a subtle abstract wave motif echoing the logo (low opacity, decorative only, must not reduce text contrast/readability).

### 3. Practice areas
- Section eyebrow/label + h2 headline (e.g. "How we can help").
- Four cards in a grid (2x2 on tablet/desktop, single column stacked on mobile): Divorce & Separation, Property Settlements, Parenting & Custody Arrangements, Mediation.
- Each card: short icon, bold short title, 1–2 sentence plain-English description (no legal jargon).
- Cards use `sand` or white-on-cream subtle card treatment — consistent card style, consistent height/alignment.

### 4. Meet the team
- h2 headline (e.g. "The people you'll actually be working with").
- Principal solicitor (18 years' experience) given visual priority — larger photo/card or featured first.
- Remaining three lawyers in a consistent card grid (photo placeholder, name, role/title, one short warm sentence — not a dense legal bio).
- This section should feel human and approachable — avoid stiff corporate headshot styling in copy tone even if real photos aren't available yet.

### 5. How it works
- h2 headline (e.g. "What happens when you reach out").
- Simple 3-step horizontal process (stacked vertically on mobile): e.g. (1) Book your free 20-minute consult, (2) We listen and walk you through your options, (3) You decide your next step, no pressure.
- Keep this visually light — numbered steps with short labels, not paragraphs of text. This section exists to reduce fear of the unknown, not to explain legal process in detail.

### 6. Why Brightwater / testimonials
- 2–3 short, believable placeholder testimonials (fictional, clearly written in a warm, human voice — avoid generic "Great service!" filler).
- Optionally 2–3 short trust/differentiator statements if testimonials alone feel thin — but avoid repeating claims already made in the Team section.

### 7. FAQ
- Accordion-style FAQ (expand/collapse), addressing real hesitations:
  - Is the consultation really free and no-obligation?
  - What happens during the 20-minute call?
  - How do I know if Brightwater is the right fit for my situation?
  - (Add 1–2 more relevant to family law if useful — cost concerns, confidentiality, timeline expectations)
- Keep answers short, warm, plain-English — no legal disclaimers or dense paragraphs.

### 8. Final CTA section
- A calm, direct, full-width closing section repeating the primary CTA.
- Slightly different visual treatment from the hero (e.g. `sage-dark` background with cream text) to mark it as the page's closing moment.
- Include a low-friction alternative (e.g. a phone number) for anyone who doesn't want to use a form/widget.

### 9. Booking section (if not merged into Final CTA)
- This is where the Calendly inline embed widget will be placed (embed code provided separately — do not build custom booking/calendar logic).
- Wrap the embed in a clean container consistent with the site's card/section styling so it doesn't look like a foreign element dropped onto the page.

### 10. Footer
- Logo (small), brief tagline.
- Contact details (phone, email — placeholder/fictional is fine).
- Explicit mention of both service areas: Brisbane and Gold Coast.
- Simple bottom line: copyright, possibly a fictional law-society-style credential line (clearly fictional, believable, not misleading in a real-world way).

